      "title": "JEE Main 2023 (06 Apr Shift 2)"
    }
  ],
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The number of points, where the curve&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;crosses the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis, is&nbsp;_____.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now differentiating the function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;with respect to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>60</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now equating&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>144</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>26</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8776;</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>95</mn></math></p><p>Now finding the nature of function at integer value near by above value we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now plotting the graph by observing&nbsp;above values,&nbsp;we get,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4bbf06d4-950b-4ae8-99cf-74634038d164.png\" style=\"width: 299px; height: 146px;\" /></p><p>Hence, it will cross&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;times.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
